eaf"}]}],"literal":"Cherishing the celestials and feeding them sacrificial offerings, / and bringing sugarcane here, which is of rare-to-obtain tradition, / having encircled the ocean-bounded earth, / like your ancestors of ancient status, / wearing a wreath of dark palmyra on your leg with a generous beautiful heroic anklet, / holding a long spear smelling of fresh flesh in the flower-filled grove, / obtaining without fault the uncontested heritage of the country with seven written emblems, / and yet not content, desiring battle, / clashing with seven kings who have sounding-voiced drums, / going, conquering in battle, and revealing your prowess, / on that day too you were rare to singers, and today too, / did Paranar sing of you? And you, / destroying Kovalur of abundant strength, your / shoulders indeed held the fortress-destroying discus, / of the growing young palmyra from which the shamed enemies fled, / having the needle-like white petals on its crown.","translation":"Like your ancestors of ancient lineage, who cherished the celestials, fed them sacrificial offerings, brought sugarcane of rare tradition to this world, and ruled the earth encircled by the ocean, you wear a dark palmyra wreath on your leg adorned with a generous, beautiful heroic anklet. Holding a long spear smelling of fresh flesh in the flower-filled grove, you obtained without fault the uncontested heritage of the land marked with seven emblems. Yet, unsatisfied, desiring battle, you clashed with seven kings who possessed loud-sounding drums, marched, conquered them in battle, and proved your prowess. On that day, you were difficult for singers to praise, and today too, did Paranar sing of you? You destroyed Kovalur of great strength, and your shoulders held the fortress-destroying discus, wearing the white needle-like petals from the crown of the growing young palmyra from which your shamed enemies fled.","modern":"தேவர்களைப் போற்றியும், அவர்களுக்கு வேள்வி உணவை ஊட்டியும், பெறுவதற்கரிய மரபினைக் கொண்ட கரும்பை இவ்வுலகிற்குத் தந்தும், கடல் சூழ்ந்த நிலப்பகுதியை ஆண்ட உமது முன்னோர்களைப் போல, கொடைத்தன்மையும் அழகிய வீரக்கழலும் அணிந்த காலில் கரிய பனைமாலையைச் சூடி, பூக்கள் நிறைந்த சோலையில் புதிய புலால் நாற்றமுடைய நீண்ட வேலை ஏந்தி, ஏழு இலச்சினைகள் பொறித்த நாட்டின் உரிமையை எவ்விதக் குற்றமுமின்றிப் பெற்றும் அமைதியடையாமல், போரை விரும்பி, முழங்கும் முரசினைக் கொண்ட ஏழு அரசர்களோடு மாறுபட்டுச் சென்று, போரில் வென்று உமது ஆற்றலை வெளிப்படுத்திய அன்றைய நாளிலும் பாடுவோர்க்கு அரியவனாக இருந்தாய்; இன்றும் பரணர் உன்னைப் பாடினார் போலும்! வலிமை மிக்க கோவலூரை அழித்து, உமது கோட்டையை அழிக்கும் சக்கரத்தை ஏந்திய தோள்களில், அஞ்சியோடிய பகைவர்களின் வளரும் இளம்பனையின் உச்சியிலிருந்த ஊசி போன்ற வெண்மையான பனையோலையைச் சூடியுள்ளாயே!","explanation":"The poet Avvaiyar is praising King Adhiyaman Neduman Anji. She extols his glorious ancestry, who brought sugarcane to the world and performed sacrifices. She describes how he was not satisfied with his inherited kingdom and went on to defeat seven allied kings. Now, he has destroyed the strong fort of Kovalur (belonging to Kari). The imagery of the white palmyra leaf taken from the enemy's grove symbolizes his victory and the humiliation of his foes.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.5],[0.5,0.9],[0.9,1.1],[1.1,1.4],[1.4,3.0],[3.0,3.6],[3.6,3.6],[3.6,4.0],[4.0,4.3],[4.3,5.6],[5.6,6.0],[6.0,6.2],[6.2,6.4],[6.4,7.3],[7.3,7.5],[7.5,7.8],[7.8,8.0],[8.0,8.4],[9.12,9.6],[9.6,10.2],[10.2,10.3],[10.3,10.7],[10.7,12.0],[12.0,12.2],[12.2,12.7],[12.7,13.2],[13.2,13.3],[13.3,13.8],[13.8,13.8],[13.8,13.8],[13.8,16.3],[16.3,17.4],[17.4,17.5],[17.5,18.12],[18.24,19.1],[19.84,20.54],[20.54,21.04],[21.16,21.52],[21.52,21.84],[21.84,22.94],[22.94,23.44],[23.44,23.74],[23.74,23.94],[23.94,24.24],[24.24,24.84],[24.84,26.04],[26.04,26.34],[26.34,27.04],[27.04,27.14],[27.14,28.24],[28.24,28.34],[28.34,28.84],[28.84,29.44],[29.44,29.64],[29.64,30.64],[30.64,30.94],[30.94,30.94],[30.94,31.44],[31.44,31.84],[31.84,32.64],[32.64,32.74],[32.74,32.84],[32.84